  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Valdecoxib, a COX-2 inhibitor painkiller, was used to treat osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, and pain such as dysmenorrhea. It has been withdrawn from the market, including its authorised products in the European Union, and is no longer in use.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q347613&quot;>Wikidata Q347613</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>valdecoxib</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>M01AH03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00580&quot;>DB00580</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/119607&quot;>119607</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:63634&quot;>63634</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q347613&quot;>Q347613</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C16H14N2O3S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>314.359 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
